{#- The masthead, to the design handoff of 2026-08-02. Sticky, dark, three things in one
   row: the wordmark, a section indicator written by the homepage's scroll spy, and the
   menu button. The panel opens directly below that row.

   The handoff's panel has two columns, JUMP TO and THE BRIEF. It carries three here,
   because the prototype was built against sample content and this site has real pages:
   dropping Numbers, Atlas, the quarterly rooms and About would orphan them. The grid is
   the handoff's auto-fit, so a third column costs nothing and reflows the same way.
   THE BRIEF column is _data/footernav.js, which is also what the footer prints, so the
   menu and the footer cannot drift apart. -#}
<header class="mast">
  <div class="mast-row">
    <a class="brand" href="/">THE MEXICO <span class="u">BRIEF</span></a>
    <div class="mast-sec" id="mast-sec" aria-live="polite"></div>
    <button class="menu-btn" type="button" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="menu-panel" aria-label="Menu"><span></span><span></span></button>
  </div>
  <div class="menu-panel" id="menu-panel" hidden>
    <div class="menu-grid">
      <div class="menu-col">
        <span class="menu-h">Jump to</span>
        <a href="/#sec-brief">The brief</a>
        <a href="/#sec-numbers">What moved</a>
        <a href="/#sec-stories">Today’s stories</a>
        <a href="/#sec-week">This week</a>
        <a href="/#sec-coming">Coming up</a>
        <a href="/#sec-econ">Where the economy stands</a>
      </div>
      <div class="menu-col">
        <span class="menu-h">Go deeper</span>
        <a href="/atlas.html">Atlas</a>
        {%- for group in nav %}{% if group.menu %}{% for block in group.menu %}{% for link in block.links %}
        <a href="{{ link.href }}">{{ link.label }}</a>{% endfor %}{% endfor %}{% endif %}{% endfor %}
        <a href="/about.html">About</a>
      </div>
      <div class="menu-col menu-col-quiet">
        <span class="menu-h">The brief</span>
        {%- for item in footernav %}
        <a href="{{ item.href }}">{{ item.label }}</a>{% endfor %}
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</header>
